  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given a set SSS, which is a subset of {1,2,…,N}\\{1, 2, \\ldots, N\\}{1,2,…,N}.\n\nConsider a permutation P1,P2,…,PNP_1, P_2, \\ldots, P_NP1​,P2​,…,PN​ of the integers 111 through NNN. The cost of this permutation is the number of indices i&gt;1i \\gt 1i&gt;1 such that PiP_iPi​ is divisible by Pi−1P_{i-1}Pi−1​ and PiPi−1∈S\\frac{P_i}{P_{i-1}} \\in SPi−1​Pi​​∈S.\n\nFor each kkk between 000 and N−1N-1N−1 (inclusive), find the number of permutations with cost kkk. Since these numbers may be large, compute them modulo 998,244,353998,244,353998,244,353.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤N≤401 \\le N \\le 401≤N≤40",
      "TTT contains only characters '0' and '1'",
      "Subtasks**Subtask #1 (10 points):** N≤15N \\le 15N≤15"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "The first line of the input contains a single integer NNN.\nThe second line contains a binary string TTT with length NNN. For each valid iii, the iii-th character of TTT is '1' if i∈Si \\in Si∈S or '0' otherwise.",
    "outputFormat": "Print a single line containing NNN space-separated integers. For each kkk (0≤k&lt;N0 \\le k \\lt N0≤k&lt;N), the k+1k+1k+1-th of these integers should be the number of permutations with cost kkk, modulo 998,244,353998,244,353998,244,353.",
